{
  "input_folder": [
    "src",
    "test",
    "gen"
  ],
  "output_folder": "output",
  "write_unit_tests": true,
  "write_source_map": true,
  "libs": [
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/open-abap/open-abap-core",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/open-abap-core",
      "exclude_filter": [
        "/src/tcp/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/open-abap/express-icf-shim",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/express-icf-shim"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/oisee/open-abap-apc",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/open-abap-apc",
      "files": [
        "/src/apc/**",
        "/src/host/**"
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/abapGit/abapGit",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/abapgit",
      "files": [
        "/src/git/zcl_abapgit_git_pack.*",
        "/src/git/zcl_abapgit_git_delta.*",
        "/src/git/zcl_abapgit_git_tag.*",
        "/src/git/zcl_abapgit_git_time.*",
        "/src/git/zcl_abapgit_git_utils.*",
        "/src/git/zcl_abapgit_hash.*",
        "/src/git/zif_abapgit_git_definitions.*",
        "/src/utils/zcl_abapgit_convert.*",
        "/src/utils/zcl_abapgit_path.*",
        "/src/utils/zcl_abapgit_string_buffer.*",
        "/src/utils/zcl_abapgit_time_date.*",
        "/src/utils/zcl_abapgit_utils.*",
        "/src/utils/zif_abapgit_log.*",
        "/src/ui/progress/zif_abapgit_progress.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_html_viewer.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zcl_abapgit_html_viewer_gui.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zcl_abapgit_gui_event.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_gui_event.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_gui_event_handler.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_gui_services.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_gui_hotkeys.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_gui_hotkey_ctl.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_gui_renderable.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zif_abapgit_html.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zcl_abapgit_html.*",
        "/src/ui/core/zcl_abapgit_html_parts.*",
        "/src/utils/zcl_abapgit_string_map.*",
        "/src/objects/aff_types/*",
        "/src/zcx_abapgit_exception.*",
        "/src/zcx_abapgit_not_found.*",
        "/src/zcx_abapgit_type_not_supported.*",
        "/src/zif_abapgit_definitions.*",
        "/src/zif_abapgit_version.*",
        "/deps/trobjtype.dtel.xml",
        "/deps/trnspace.tabl.xml",
        "/deps/dokil.tabl.xml"
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/oisee/open-abap-gui",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/open-abap-gui",
      "files": [
        "/src/**",
        "/framework/**"
      ],
      "exclude_filter": [
        "/framework/http/",
        "/framework/assets/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/open-abap/open-abap-odata",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/open-abap-odata",
      "files": [
        "/src/oo/**",
        "/src/ddic/**",
        "/src/exceptions/**",
        "/src/internal/**"
      ],
      "exclude_filter": [
        "(#iwbep#if_mgw_odata_(action|parameter)\\.intf|zcl_oao_action\\.clas)\\."
      ]
    },
    {
      "url": "https://github.com/sbcgua/ajson",
      "folder": "/.local/lars/ajson",
      "files": [
        "/src/core/**"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "options": {
    "ignoreSyntaxCheck": false,
    "addFilenames": true,
    "addCommonJS": true,
    "unknownTypes": "compileError",
    "setup": {
      "filename": "../test/setup.mjs",
      "preFunction": "setup"
    },
    "skip": [
      {
        "object": "ZCL_ZOSD_TEST_DEMO",
        "class": "ltcl_zosd_test_demo",
        "method": "deliberate_failure"
      },
      {
        "object": "ZCL_L3_FLEET_PROOF",
        "class": "ltcl_proof",
        "method": "governor_glass",
        "_why": "real jobs and human continuation need a file DB and worker; test/dsl-l3.mjs runs this proof with both, as the other job proofs"
      },
      {
        "object": "ZCL_L3_FLEET_PROOF",
        "class": "ltcl_proof",
        "method": "mode_p",
        "_why": "background jobs need STG_DB=file and a dialog step per method, and nothing runs a job in this loop; test/dsl-l3.mjs runs the whole class, mode_p included, with both and a worker (docs/dsl-l3.md, Proof)"
      },
      {
        "object": "ZCL_L3_FLEET_PROOF",
        "class": "ltcl_proof",
        "method": "stages_mode_p",
        "_why": "as mode_p: the two stages' jobs need STG_DB=file, a dialog step per method and a worker; test/dsl-l3.mjs runs it with all three (docs/dsl-l3.md, Stages, filters and a schedule)"
      },
      {
        "object": "ZCL_L3_FLEET_PROOF",
        "class": "ltcl_proof",
        "method": "sim_twin",
        "_why": "as mode_p: the simulated twin runs in real jobs the doctor submits again, which needs STG_DB=file, a dialog step per method and a worker; test/dsl-l3.mjs runs it with all three (docs/dsl-l3.md, Simulated twin)"
      },
      {
        "object": "ZCL_L3_FLEET_PROOF",
        "class": "ltcl_proof",
        "method": "doctor_heals",
        "_why": "as mode_p: the doctor submits a pile again as a real job, which needs STG_DB=file, a dialog step per method and a worker; test/dsl-l3.mjs runs it with all three (docs/dsl-l3.md, Resilience)"
      },
      {
        "object": "ZCL_L3_FLEET_PROOF",
        "class": "ltcl_proof",
        "method": "doctor_keeps_run_values",
        "_why": "as doctor_heals: the doctor's resubmit and stage 2 run as real jobs; test/dsl-l3.mjs runs it with a worker (docs/dsl-l3.md, Settings)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "exclude_filter": [
    "/test/e2e/",
    "/src/.*/cockpit/",
    "/test/fixtures/",
    "\\.mjs$",
    "\\.cjs$",
    "\\.sapc\\.xml$",
    "\\.samc\\.xml$",
    "\\.samc\\.model\\.json$",
    "\\.samc\\.decl\\.json$",
    "\\.ddls\\.",
    "\\.srvd\\.",
    "/gen/rap/bindings\\.json$",
    "\\.stg\\.yaml$",
    "\\.l2\\.yaml$",
    "\\.l3\\.yaml$",
    "\\.trace(?:\\.meta)?\\.json$"
  ],
  "_not_in_system": "Which of the exclusions above also mean 'this is not an object of this system'. The rest mean only 'the transpiler cannot read this file', which says nothing about whether the object exists: a CDS view is excluded by \\.ddls\\. and is very much an object here. The distinction is intent and cannot be inferred from the pattern - three attempts at inferring it were wrong in three different directions - so it is stated. Every entry must also be in exclude_filter, and test/store-exclusions.mjs checks that, so the two cannot drift. test/fixtures joined the list on 2026-09-19, after a check run over the whole tree complained, correctly about the object and falsely about the system, that a fixture selects from a table the system does not have: the fixture is not in the system, and the one test that read it as one now reads a program that is.",
  "not_in_system": [
    "/src/.*/cockpit/",
    "/test/fixtures/",
    "\\.stg\\.yaml$",
    "\\.l2\\.yaml$",
    "\\.l3\\.yaml$",
    "\\.trace(?:\\.meta)?\\.json$",
    "\\.samc\\.model\\.json$",
    "\\.samc\\.decl\\.json$"
  ]
}
